<h2>What's new?</h2>
<p>Journelly v1.5's biggest gain is performance. It should bring you an overall snappier experience, especially on larger journals. This release also brings new search features.</p>
<h3>Faster with large journals</h3>
<p>A user reported migrating about ten years of journaling from <a href="https://dayoneapp.com/">Day One</a> into Journelly: over 3,600 entries and thousands of images, converted from a Day One JSON export into Journelly's plain text format. With that much content, typing and navigating became sluggish.</p>
<p>Journelly v1.5 brings a nice round of performance work, so typing, saving, and navigating are now smoother for journals of all sizes. If you're considering a similar move, Journelly should now comfortably handle years of entries.</p>
<h3>On This Day</h3>
<p>When you have entries from today's date in previous years, a new button appears on screen. Tap it to see what you were up to on this very day, years ago. The little badge shows how many matching entries were found.</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/journelly-1-5-released/new-button.jpg" alt=""></p>
<p>Not your cup of tea? Hide the button via &quot;Menu &gt; View &gt; On This Day.&quot;</p>
<h3>Search by date</h3>
<p>Search now understands dates via a new <code>on:</code> filter:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>on:2024</code> finds everything from 2024.</li>
<li><code>on:2024-11</code> finds November 2024.</li>
<li><code>on:November</code> finds every November, any year.</li>
<li><code>on:&quot;November 3&quot;</code> (or <code>on:11-03</code>) finds every November 3rd, any year.</li>
<li><code>on:&quot;November 3, 2024&quot;</code> (or <code>on:2024-11-03</code>) finds that very day.</li>
</ul>
<p>Dates can be written in your own language too (<code>on:&quot;3 de noviembre&quot;</code>, <code>on:&quot;11月3日&quot;</code>), and can be combined with regular search terms and hashtags (<code>on:2024 #travel</code>). Matching dates are highlighted in entry titles.</p>
<h3>Pick a date from the calendar</h3>
<p>Prefer a calendar view? Tap the calendar button in the search bar to pick a day to search for. Days with entries are marked with a dot, offering a handy way to see when you wrote.</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/journelly-1-5-released/search.jpg" alt=""></p>
